From fe8ed4f04bcd6f0cac4c921bb967c2830e1bd565 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Krueckel <hi@felkru.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:22:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 48/53] Tabs restored across VS Code windows via the host

On the web, Warp's session restoration has no SQLite, so the layout (tabs,
splits, titles, each pane's directory) and finished blocks go to the host
page, which keeps them in the extension's warp.sqlite shared by all VS Code
windows. At startup Warp restores from the host's latest layout and opens
each restored pane's shell in its saved directory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
